hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27999","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muawiyah, narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Isa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abd Allah, he being a truthful man, from a woman of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a road to the mosque, foul-smelling; how shall we do when it rains upon us. He said: Is there not after it a road better than it. She said: I said: Yes. He said: Then this is for that."
"28000","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Israil informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from a woman of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, that she said: I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I pass in a road not pleasant. He said: Is not what is after it better than it. She said: Yes. He said: This removes that."
